  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Let \\(n\\) be the number of real values of \\(p\\) for which the roots of\n\n\\[ x^2-px+p=0 \\]\n\nare equal. Then \\(n\\) equals:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "a finite number greater than \\(2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "an infinitely large number"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": "2"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1964-p7.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Equal roots require \\[(-p)^2-4p=p(p-4)=0.\\] Thus \\(p=0\\) or \\(p=4,\\) giving two real values.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Equal roots make the discriminant zero",
        "Solve \\(p^2-4p=0\\)"
      ],
